16:["$","aside",null,{"className":"docs_toc__B_lbZ","aria-label":"On this page","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"ON THIS PAGE"}],[["$","a","name-the-logical-effect",{"href":"#name-the-logical-effect","children":"Name the logical effect"}],["$","a","diagram-the-lost-acknowledgement",{"href":"#diagram-the-lost-acknowledgement","children":"Diagram: the lost acknowledgement"}],["$","a","be-precise-about-guarantees",{"href":"#be-precise-about-guarantees","children":"Be precise about guarantees"}],["$","a","try-it",{"href":"#try-it","children":"Try it"}],["$","a","check-your-understanding",{"href":"#check-your-understanding","children":"Check your understanding"}],["$","a","read-further",{"href":"#read-further","children":"Read further"}]]]}]
17:["$","main",null,{"className":"docs_main__7o2m6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_articleMeta__8zYHO","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"LESSON 05 OF 8"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Systems"}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"docs_article__Ja_Vh","children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":[[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Idempotency and delivery guarantees"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":["An at-least-once broker may deliver the same logical job more than once. A worker can also finish its work and crash before acknowledging the message. Design the ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"effect"}]," to be safe under repetition rather than equating one delivery with one action."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"id":"name-the-logical-effect","children":"Name the logical effect"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":["In the export example, ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"operationId"}]," is stable across retries. Use it to name the output object, such as ",["$","code","code-1",{"children":"exports/exp_82/result.pdf"}],", and to guard the status transition. The ",["$","code","code-2",{"children":"jobId"}]," or broker receipt may change; neither is a suitable deduplication key for the business operation."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":"An idempotent result write can follow this outline:"}],"\n",["$","pre","pre-0",{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-text","children":"claim operation exp_82\nif status == succeeded: acknowledge existing result\nif status == cancelled: acknowledge without new effect\nacquire a bounded processing claim for exp_82\ncreate result at deterministic key or staging key\ncommit result reference and succeeded state conditionally\nacknowledge message\n"}]}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":"The processing claim prevents ordinary overlap, but its lease can expire. The final result write still needs a uniqueness or conditional-update rule. If creating the file has a non-repeatable side effect, use a provider idempotency key when available and retain the provider's result ID. A local “processed” flag alone cannot atomically guarantee what an external provider did."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"id":"diagram-the-lost-acknowledgement","children":"Diagram: the lost acknowledgement"}],"\n",["$","figure","p-4",{"className":"docs_studyFigure__4Js_y","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_studyFigureViewport__ZYDNN","children":["$","img","img-0",{"className":"docs_studyFigureImage__Gb2YJ","src":"/learning/async-systems/idempotency.svg","alt":"Worker A completes an export but loses its acknowledgement; Worker B sees the existing result after redelivery and acknowledges without creating a second file.","width":"920","height":"402","loading":"lazy"}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":"Worker A completes an export but loses its acknowledgement; Worker B sees the existing result after redelivery and acknowledges without creating a second file."}]]}],"\n",["$","details","pre-1",{"className":"docs_textDiagram__KfHuf","children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"Read the text version of this flow"}],["$","pre",null,{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-aosdf-diagram","children":"Worker A ──▶ writes exports/exp_82/result.pdf ──▶ commits succeeded\n                                         │\n                                         └── crash before queue ack\nQueue ──▶ redelivers exp_82 ──▶ Worker B sees succeeded ──▶ ack only\n"}]}]]}],"\n",["$","p","p-5",{"children":[["$","$L13","a-0",{"href":"/queue-delivery-lifecycle.archify.html","children":"Explore the full queue delivery diagram"}]," and look at the gap between applying an effect and acknowledgement."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"id":"be-precise-about-guarantees","children":"Be precise about guarantees"}],"\n",["$","p","p-6",{"children":["$L23"," processing can lose work but avoids broker-driven repeats. ","$L24"," prioritizes retry after uncertainty and requires duplicate-safe consumers. “Exactly once” claims usually apply within a narrow subsystem or transaction boundary; they do not magically cover an external API, object store, and database together. Describe the actual observable effect: for example, “one downloadable export per operation ID, despite duplicate queue delivery.”"]}],"\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c"],false]}]]}],"$L2d"]}]
